## For the lead

1. **After-core check days (calendar pass).** The mid-year check is school day 80 (week 16), off every grade 7 core
   check day; the year-end check is school day 158 in the finals week. Pick for the pass: keep day 80 unless another
   after-core grade 7 check lands on it.
2. **Grade 8 unit numbers in the Seams.** The grade 6 frame's units are cited (its Handed on table matches this
   frame's rows); grade 8's frame was not on disk when this was written, so the Handed on table cites grade 8 rows.
   Pick: the seam read adds grade 8's unit numbers and checks its Picked up table against this one.
3. **Code review's handoff.** g7-collab-text hands on to no row, though grade 8's text project hands its program to
   a partner to read and explain. Pick: Row changes 1 (both ends).
4. **The partial base edition and store folder.** As the pilot's For the lead 4: Cory confirms the archived edition;
   the lead loads key stage 3 (Year 8 "Introduction to Python programming", Year 9 "Python programming with sequences
   of data", Year 8 "Layers of computing systems") into S:\CurioClass-sources\teach-computing-curriculum with
   MANIFEST.csv, reads each file's own license line, and runs the per-unit third-party check. Lessons 5 and 6 of the
   Year 9 sequences unit and the Year 9 data science unit are offered to the grade 8 frame.
5. **Tool asks.** A picture-sorter model in the page (train, test, accuracy, no camera, no upload) and a toy network
   with breakable links; both join the editor's build list (STANDARD.md "Our own editor") as page tools, not
   accounts.
6. **Source list.** docs/APPROACH-SOURCES.md: the GIDA CARE Principles, the US Indigenous Data Sovereignty Network,
   the Native Nations Institute, NISTIR 8280, the 2020 speech recognition study, the NTIA Internet Use Survey, the
   House Oversight Committee's 2016 OPM report, the EPA electronics page and the BLS Occupational Outlook Handbook.

## Source map

The partial base for grade 7 is the archived edition of England's Teach Computing Curriculum, key stage 3
(raspberrypi.org/curriculum/archived/key-stage-3; Year 8 is the grade 7 age; resources dated 2023). Placed from the
public unit pages (lesson titles), opened 2026-11-25; every unit opened shows six lessons. The publisher teaches each
unit's lessons in number order; where this frame splits or reorders a unit, the row says why. Each adapted lesson
keeps its idea, is rewritten in our words for an American grade 7, replaces named apps with our own editor and page
tools, and is credited once a day. Check days are ours, never a kept lesson.

