## Seams

### Picked up from Grade 7 computer science

Every grade 8 row assumes grade 7 rows only, the year before, so each opens as a retrieval task inside its first day
(lesson 16), never as a readiness check; the scope gate's count governs. Each row's last use is the grade 7 computer
science unit named below (docs/courses/computer-science-grade-7/frame.md, course days from data/plans/calendar.csv).
If a school left out grade 7's unit 4 (its Swap or leave out bullet), g8-ml-evaluate and g8-modify-for-bias open with
a readiness check instead, in the last ten minutes of unit 3's respond day (day 42), as the grade 7 frame says.

| Row picked up (grade 7 unit, course days) | What it hands on | Row here | Unit and day it opens as retrieval |
|---|---|---|---|
| g7-internet-resilience (unit 5, days 44 to 55) | Find another path around a cut node or link; routers and servers | g8-network-failure | 1, day 1 |
| g7-cia-effects (unit 5, days 44 to 55) | The confidentiality, integrity and availability triangle and the effect on people of a side ignored | g8-cyber-attacks | 1, day 3 |
| g7-system-requirements (unit 5, days 44 to 55) | Requirements written for a given family or shop, two options and a tradeoff | g8-choose-a-system | 1, day 6 |
| g7-access-differences (unit 5, days 44 to 55) | Barriers to the same system by ability, internet, language, cost and place | g8-design-for-all | 1, day 8 |
| g7-design-with-variables (unit 1, days 1 to 10) | A flowchart and pseudocode design with variables of more than one type, built in text | g8-text-project | 2, day 14 |
| g7-lists (unit 2, days 11 to 23) | A list as a named box with numbered slots, looped over, the list-diagram | g8-text-project | 2, day 15 |
| g7-analyze-code (unit 1, days 1 to 10) | Mark the role of each loop, choice, variable and procedure in a twenty-line program and predict output | g8-text-project; g8-evaluate-ai-code | 2, day 15; 4, day 50 |
| g7-reference-docs (unit 2, days 11 to 23) | Find and use a function from the language's reference page | g8-attribution | 2, day 21 |
| g7-test-refine (unit 2, days 11 to 23) | A planned test-table, one fix at a time, a change log and a recheck | g8-refine-for-users | 2, day 25 |
| g7-collab-text (unit 2, days 11 to 23) | A peer code review with a kind, specific checklist | g8-text-project (the grade 7 frame's Row changes 1, which this frame agrees with; Row changes below) | 2, day 24 |
| g7-sort-filter-groups (unit 3, days 24 to 31) | Group and summarize a fifty-row table with a tool | g8-relationships | 3, day 31 |
| g7-viz-choices (unit 3, days 24 to 31) | How a chart's design choices change what a reader concludes; the fairest chart | g8-relationships; g8-investigation-summary | 3, day 31; 3, day 35 |
| g7-personal-data (unit 3, days 24 to 31) | Benefits and risks of personal data and metadata collection, ownership and consent | g8-biased-decisions | 3, day 39 |
| g7-improve-training-data (unit 4, days 34 to 43) | Train, test, add better examples and non-examples, measure accuracy again | g8-ml-evaluate | 4, day 43 |
| g7-examine-algorithm-harm (unit 4, days 34 to 43) | Everyday algorithms as cases of benefit and harm, with evidence | g8-modify-for-bias | 4, day 47 |
| g7-pick-approach (unit 4, days 34 to 43) | Choose step-by-step, rule-based, learned from data, or a mix, and justify it | g8-ai-tool-day | 4, day 49 |
| g7-when-to-use-ai (unit 6, days 56 to 62) | When an AI or other emerging technology suits a task, by strengths, limits and energy | g8-emerging-design; g8-emerging-debate | 5, day 55; 5, day 58 |
| g7-impact-history (unit 6, days 56 to 62) | Intended and unintended effects of a historical computing technology on a timeline | g8-history-case; g8-emerging-debate | 5, day 57; 5, day 58 |
| g7-automation-work (unit 6, days 56 to 62) | Jobs changed by automation, tasks replaced and created, two views | g8-career-sketch | 5, day 61 |

Each row above lists the grade 8 row in its hands_on in data/progressions/computer-science.csv, and each grade 8 row
lists it in its assumes, except g7-collab-text, whose link is the row change both frames propose. MS-SOC-CE-44 (g8-career-sketch) was owned in grade 6 (g6-careers-ct), but the row assumes
only g7-automation-work, its year-before use.

### Handed on to Grade 9 computer science and beyond

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up | What it does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| g8-network-failure: redraw a map after a failure and add a backup link | 1 | g9-network-sketch | Read a school network diagram and trace one request through it |
| g8-cyber-attacks: common attacks matched to the triangle side and a prevention | 1 | g9-security-measures | Compare security measures and their cost to users |
| g8-choose-a-system: choose a system against another group's requirements, justified line by line | 1 | g9-operating-systems; g9-device-limits | The operating system as a manager layer; a device tested against a task |
| g8-design-for-all: a team's design change for different users' needs, tested | 1 | g11-infrastructure-impact | How computing infrastructure affects access |
| g8-text-project: a designed, built, traced text project with variables, a list and a procedure | 2 | g9-structures-program; g9-design-with-structures; g9-optimize-procedures; g9-modular | Lists and key-value records, structures chosen for a design, procedures with parameters, modules |
| g8-attribution: when credit and permission are needed, and a credit line in code | 2 | g10-apis-docs | Credit a library and its documentation page in a comment |
